.TH STAGERIG 1 "October 2026" "StageRig" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
StageRig \- live\-performance plugin host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B StageRig
.RI [ setup.stagerig.json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B StageRig
hosts VST3, CLAP, LV2 and LADSPA instruments and effects for playing live,
for keyboards and for audio. An
.I input
is either a keyboard (a MIDI device and channel) or an audio input (channels
of the audio interface: a microphone, a guitar, a hardware synth). Each has 128
programs selected by MIDI Program Change: on a keyboard a program holds one or
more instruments with key and velocity ranges, insert effects and MIDI
controller mappings; on an audio input it is an effect chain. Every input lands
on an output, a pair of the interface's channels, with master effects. Songs combine a program per input with a tempo, and set lists order
the songs for a footswitch to step through.
.PP
A built\-in web app lets a tablet or phone on the same network change programs,
follow the set list, show charts, and operate any loaded plugin's own
interface.
.PP
Every plugin runs in its own
.BR stagerig\-plugin\-host (1)
process, so a plugin that crashes or hangs takes only itself down.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I setup.stagerig.json
Open this setup instead of the one used last. Setups saved by earlier versions
under the name Performer
.RI ( *.performer.json )
are accepted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/StageRig/StageRig.settings
Window, audio device, plugin scan results and options.
.TP
.I ~/.config/StageRig/autosave.stagerig.json
The rolling autosave of the open setup.
.TP
.I ~/.config/StageRig/mapping\-templates.json
Saved per\-plugin MIDI mapping templates.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STAGERIG_PLUGIN_HOST
Path of the plugin host executable, when it is not installed beside
.BR StageRig .
.SH NOTES
Mirroring a plugin's interface to a tablet needs
.BR x11vnc (1),
.BR websockify (1),
.BR xdotool (1)
and noVNC. Charts in PDF form are prepared with
.BR pdftoppm (1).
The full manual is under Help in the application.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stagerig\-plugin\-host (1)
.PP
https://github.com/dguedry/stagerig
